# duti defaults for Lambert's macOS machines
#
# Format: <bundle-id> <UTI-or-extension> <role>
# Roles: viewer | editor | all | none
#
# Apply with:  just apply-file-associations
# Or directly: duti ~/.config/duti/defaults.duti
#
# Philosophy (from retros/decisions/2026-07-23-app-strategy-macdown-and-general-tools.md):
#   Rendering / passive viewing → general host (Chrome, Preview).
#   Editing / annotating       → programmable substrate (Emacs).
#
# This file is intentionally sparse. We only codify what has been explicitly
# decided. Other candidate extensions (.txt, .json, .yaml, .html, images, PDFs)
# are currently claimed by sensible defaults (TextEdit/Emacs/Finicky/Preview) —
# a codification pass will happen after we discuss each one.

# ─── Markdown: Chrome (with Markdown Viewer extension) ──────────────────────
# Retro decision (2026-07-23): `.md` should render immediately without a context
# switch into Emacs authoring UI. Chrome + Markdown Viewer extension does this.
# Emacs is still the correct home for authoring — this only affects the
# double-click / `open` path.
com.google.Chrome  .md  all
